        "id": "p53-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\int_{-1}^{1}x^2(x^3+1)^4\\,dx$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{32}{15}$",
          "worked": "The inner function is $x^3+1$, with derivative $3x^2$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int_{-1}^{1}x^2(x^3+1)^4\\,dx&=\\frac13\\int_{-1}^{1}3x^2(x^3+1)^4\\,dx\\\\&=\\left[\\frac{(x^3+1)^5}{15}\\right]_{-1}^{1}\\\\&=\\frac{2^5-0^5}{15}\\\\&=\\frac{32}{15}.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p53-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\int_0^1\\frac{x}{(5x^2+1)^3}\\,dx$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{7}{144}$",
          "worked": "The inner function is $5x^2+1$, with derivative $10x$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int_0^1\\frac{x}{(5x^2+1)^3}\\,dx&=\\frac1{10}\\int_0^1 10x(5x^2+1)^{-3}\\,dx\\\\&=\\left[-\\frac{1}{20(5x^2+1)^2}\\right]_0^1\\\\&=-\\frac1{720}+\\frac1{20}\\\\&=\\frac{35}{720}\\\\&=\\frac7{144}.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p53-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$$\\int_0^{\\frac12}x\\sqrt{1-4x^2}\\,dx$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{1}{12}$",
          "worked": "The inner function is $1-4x^2$, with derivative $-8x$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int_0^{\\frac12}x\\sqrt{1-4x^2}\\,dx&=-\\frac18\\int_0^{\\frac12}(-8x)(1-4x^2)^{\\frac12}\\,dx\\\\&=\\left[-\\frac1{12}(1-4x^2)^{\\frac32}\\right]_0^{\\frac12}\\\\&=0-\\left(-\\frac1{12}\\right)\\\\&=\\frac1{12}.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p53-q9-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$$\\int_{-3}^{-1}(x+5)(x^2+10x+3)^2\\,dx$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$936$",
          "worked": "The inner function is $x^2+10x+3$, with derivative $2x+10=2(x+5)$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int_{-3}^{-1}(x+5)(x^2+10x+3)^2\\,dx&=\\frac12\\int_{-3}^{-1}(2x+10)(x^2+10x+3)^2\\,dx\\\\&=\\left[\\frac{(x^2+10x+3)^3}{6}\\right]_{-3}^{-1}\\\\&=\\frac{(-6)^3-(-18)^3}{6}\\\\&=\\frac{-216+5832}{6}\\\\&=936.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
